# Generated artifacts (runtime output — never commit)
dist/
logs/
# Exception (PR #548 review): committed external-referee run logs are
# EVIDENCE, not runtime output -- REPRODUCE_GATE_RECORD's log_path must
# be git-tracked so a reviewer outside this machine can open it (the
# whole point of the fill-contract test in
# tests/test_coax_two_port_referee_header.py). The broad "logs/" rule
# above would otherwise silently swallow this directory too.
# The coax two-port referee's own run-3 evidence (issue #489 stage 3)
# used to need the exception here at
# validation/research/coax_two_port/logs/ -- it moved to
# validation/crossval/_21_coax_two_port_referee_logs/ on promotion
# (2026-08-04, PI decision, issue #489 comment), a directory name that
# does NOT match the bare "logs/" pattern above, so no negation is
# needed for it (verified: git check-ignore reports it untracked-by-rule).
# The MSL phase referee's own run-1 evidence (issue #490 lane 2) used to
# need the same exception here at validation/research/msl_phase_referee/
# logs/ -- it moved to validation/crossval/_20_msl_phase_referee_logs/ on
# promotion (2026-08-04, #490 reviewer judgment), a directory name that
# does NOT match the bare "logs/" pattern above, so no negation is needed
# for it (verified: git check-ignore reports it untracked-by-rule).
**/*.png
!docs/guide/images/*.png
!docs/public/examples/assets/*.png
!docs/crossval/figures/*.png
**/*.gif
**/benchmark_results.json
examples/*.json

# VESSL cluster log mirrors (operational; not physics evidence)
docs/vessl-logs/
scripts/diagnostics/_artifacts/*.npz

# PyPI upload credentials — never commit
.pypi
.pypirc

# Gallery v3 figure-builder intermediate field caches (regenerated on demand)
scripts/_patch_v3_cache.npz
scripts/_patch_field_cache.npz
